  (base/rule
   :name "Stasis"
   :image "images/rule-stasis.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly
   :summary
    "Stasis represents a time freeze effect. Add this to related Damage
     Minor - Skipping
     Major - Stuck. Impaired
     Critical - Anchored. Slow:1 Impaired
     Extreme - Stopped. Slow:2 Immobilized
     * Head, Chest, Abdomen - Choking:3 Dying
     Action - Each Damage dealt to Binder reduces Severity by 1
     Escape - IF out of reach
     Dead - A Unit that dies by Stasis instead is perfectly preserved until released")
  (base/rule
   :name "Storytelling"
   :summary
    "Storytelling is composed of multiple nested parts:
     * Universe - A distinct universal setting and timeline. Different Universes can potentially crossover. Significant Milestones form the History of this Universe. A Universe contains any number of Campaigns.
     * Campaign - A set of connected Stories with an overall introduction, progression, and finale. A well structured Campaign will take characters on a journey of physical, mental, and psychological challenges, losses, and growth. Different Campaigns can take place at different time periods. A movie trilogy would form a campaign. A Campaign contains a series of Stories.
     * Story - A set of connected Chapters with a distinct introduction, progression, and conclusion. A well structured Story will include classic story structures such as Hero's Journey, 3 Act Structure, Dan Harmon's Story Circle, etc. A Story contains a series of Chapters.
     * Chapter - A distinct Story narrative that progresses the Story. A Chapter should be analogous to a game session. A Chapter can start and end at any point, usually for dramatic effect including cliffhangers. A well structured Chapter will include classic story structures like 3 Act Structure, 5 Room Dungeon, etc. A character, perspective, time shift may occur between Chapters. A Chapter contains a series of Plots and Acts. When all Plots OR all Acts resolve then the Chapter resolves with partial or complete success or failure.
     * Plot - A distinct dramatic situation occurring at a specific Scene. This may be an actual plot that someone is attempting or some other not ideal situation that is progressing. As in Tarot, this represents the future if the Characters do not Act. Each Plot contains a series of Encounters. When all Encounters are resolved, the Plot progresses (The Plot Thickens).
     * Encounter - A distinct obstacle/challenge to the Characters. It can be physical, intellectual, psychological, or social (a blend of each type is ideal). Encounters are distractions from or obstacles to completing the Charaters' Goals. Encounters may be scripted or random. Examples include Darkness, Smoke, Fire, Barrier, Locked Door, Terrain, Wildlife, Crowds, Social Obligations, Criminals, Law Enforcement, Rivals, Enemies, and Monsters.
     * Act - The opportunity for Character agency and action during the Chapter. As in Tarot, this represents the future if the Characters successfully Act. Each Act contains a series of Goals. When all Goals are resolved, the Act progresses.
     * Goal - A distinct desired outcome for the Characters. Like Encounters, it can be physical, intellectual, phychological, or social (a blend of each type is ideal). Goals may be scripted or random. Examples include obtaining an item, finding a person, acquiring information, travelling to/escaping from a location, convincing/defeating opposition, rescuing/protecting someone/something, solving a mystery.")

  (base/rule
   :name "Study"
   :deck "Reference"
   :summary
    "Tests may be made easier by carefully studying the problem.A test may be attempted after each Study level. Study requires specialized equipment (eg an Alchemical Kit). Beyond 6 Hours, outside [Research] will be necessary.
     * Level:+1 - 2 Minutes
     * Level:+2 - 10 Minutes
     * Level:+3 - 1 Hour
     * Level:+4 - 6 Hours")
  (base/rule
   :name "Subtle"
   :summary
    "Subtle Abilities are not obviously linked to the user.
     * [Blatant] is the opposite of [Subtle]")
  (base/rule
   :name "Suit"
   :summary
    "Each Suit represents a Stat:
     * Wands - Power. Body
     * Coins - Planning. Mind
     * Cups - Perseverance. Will
     * Swords - Skill. Speed")
  (base/rule
   :name "Summon"
   :summary
    "Instantly opens a hazy portal to a specific being or object that has previously been connected to the user with a [Binding]. A summoned being may choose not to cross through the portal.")
  (base/rule
   :name "Summoning"
   :summary
    "A long ritual that opens a hazy portal to a specific being. This is much slower than a [Summon] and is typically used when a [Binding] does not exist. The summoned being may choose not to cross through the portal.")
  (base/rule
   :name "Surprise"
   :image "images/rule-surprise.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Surrounded"
   :image "images/rule-surrounded.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Target#"
   :image "images/rule-target-num.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Task"
   :image "images/rule-task.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Terms"
   :image "images/rule-terms.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Terrain:Blocking"
   :summary
    "Dangerous Terrain requires Skill Tests to travel safely or take damage
     * [Move]:-1
     * IF a Unit moves more than 3 Spaces in the terrain in one Round THEN treat it as [Terrain:Unstable]
     * [Line of Sight]: Blocked
     * [Block]: [Skill]:+1, [Armor]:+1
     * [Evade]: [Skill]:+1")
  (base/rule
   :name "Terrain:Dangerous"
   :summary
    "Dangerous Terrain requires Skill Tests to travel safely or take damage")
  (base/rule
   :name "Terrain:Hazardous"
   :summary
    "Hazardous Terrain does damage to anyone inside")
  (base/rule
   :name "Terrain:Obscuring"
   :summary
    "Obscuring Terrain proves Cover
     * [Cover]:+25% within the Terrain
     * Line of Sight is blocked beyond the Terrain")
  (base/rule
   :name "Terrain:Rough"
   :summary
    "Difficult Terrain slows movement
     * [Move]:-1")
  (base/rule
   :name "Terrain:Unstable"
   :summary
    "Dangerous Terrain requires Skill Tests to avoid falling down")
  (base/rule
   :name "Thirst"
   :image "images/rule-thirst.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Thorns"
   :summary
    "Create an [Aura] in your Space that can attack anything inside
     * Once per Round: Use the [Ability] to attack a Rival within the Aura without spend any [Move]
     * [Continuous]")
  (base/rule
   :name "Time:Afternoon")
  (base/rule
   :name "Time:Evening")
  (base/rule
   :name "Time:Morning")
  (base/rule
   :name "Time:Night")
  (base/rule
   :name "Tone Pivot"
   :summary
    "H - Silence/Noise - A threat is made. Everyone goes silent looking for who made it")
  (base/rule
   :name "Totem"
   :summary
    "A Totem is a focus for remotely manifesting a [Power]. Powers may used as if the Totem were the User")
  (base/rule
   :name "Touch")
  (base/rule
   :name "Transformed"
   :image "images/rule-transformed.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly
   :summary
    "Transformed represents body transformation. Add this to related Damage
     Minor - Altered
     Major - Turning. Impaired
     Critical - Mutating. Stress:1 Immobilized
     Extreme - Remade. Stress:2
     Damage - Each Damage dealt to Transformer reduces Severity by 1
     Escape - IF out of Transformer reach")
  (base/rule
   :name "Transport"
   :titles "Mount, Vehicle"
   :summary
    "Anything you can ride is a Transport
     eg Horses, Cars, Planes
     * Driver - Spend an Action each Round to control
     * Passenger - IF unstable or in Combat THEN Spend an Action to remain stable")
  (base/rule
   :name "Treat:Wounds"
   :titles "Healing"
   :summary
    "Repairing damage to living creatures is difficult and dangerous
     * Time - 
     * Surgery - Perform a [Task] vs 3x[Severity]. If you lack a relevant [Ability], [Specialty] or perfect conditions it is at [Disadvantage]. Beginning the procedure creates a [Severity]:1 Wound at the location. Each failure causes [Blood Loss]:2")
  (base/rule
   :name "Unit:Guide"
   :image "images/rule-unit-guide.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Unit:Sample"
   :image "images/rule-unit-sample.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Unit#"
   :image "images/rule-unit-num.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Unskilled"
   :image "images/rule-unskilled.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Velocity"
   :image "images/rule-velocity.svg"
   :summary
    "Velocity represents the speed and momentum of fast Units. It replaces normal movement
     Round Start
      Velocity - Starts at 0
      Momentum = Velocity
     Countdown - When Count is called, MAY spend Momentum:-1 instead of Move:-1 to move straight or Drift Forward
      IF Count >= Momentum THEN not optional
     Free Actions
      Accelerate:X - Spend Move:X to gain Velocity:+1 (Min=2)
      Brake:X - Spend Move:X to lose Velocity:-1 (Min=1)")
  (base/rule
   :name "Vice"
   :summary
    "Clubs:
     Cowardly
     Reckless
     Impulsive
     Lazy
     Gluttonous
     Procrastinating
     Irresponsible
     Stubborn
     Furious
     Violent
     Wasteful
     Addicted
     Despairing

     Diamonds:
     Proud
     Arrogant
     Hubristic
     Ignorant
     Narrow-minded
     Paranoid
     Delusional
     Obsessive
     Indecisive
     Gullible
     Cynical
     Apathetic
     Foolish

     Hearts:
     Jealous
     Envious
     Hateful
     Bitter
     Spiteful
     Cruel
     Callous
     Selfish
     Vain
     Lustful
     Needy
     Sentimental
     Melancholic

     Spades:
     Dishonest  
     Deceitful
     Hypocritical
     Treacherous
     Corrupt
     Bigoted
     Intolerant
     Greedy
     Wrathful
     Vengeful
     Malicious
     Impious
     Traitorous")
  (base/rule
   :name "Virtue"
   :summary
    "Wands (Jock):
     A Competitive/Cooperative
     2 Proud/Humble
     3 Loyal/Rebellious
     4 Traditional/Open-Minded
     5 Stoic/Expressive
     6 Assertive/Thoughtful
     7 Ambitious/Satisfied
     8 Protective/Independent
     9 Outgoing/Reserved
     T Honorable/Elusive

     Coins (Nerd):
     A Idealistic/Pragmatic
     2 Pragmatic/Idealistic
     3 Frugal/Generous
     4 Open-Minded/Traditional
     5 Methodical/Creative
     6 Skeptical/Spiritual
     7 Reserved/Outgoing
     8 Thoughtful/Assertive
     9 Cautious/Brave
    	T Patient/Urgent
     J Reliable/Impulsive

     Cups (Goodie/Goodie):
     A Brave/Cautious
     2 Generous/Frugal
     3 Spiritual/Skeptical
     4 Cooperative/Competitive
     5 Humble/Proud
     5 Forgiving/Vengeful
     6 Expressive/Stoic
     7 Trusting/Suspicious
     8 Satisfied/Ambitious
     9 Disciplined/Spontaneous
     T Determined/Flexible (Consistent/Stubborn)

     Spades (Artistic/Outsider):
     A Creative/Methodical
     2 Rebellious/Loyal
     3 Vengeful/Forgiving
     4 Suspicious/Trusting
     5 Spontaneous/Disciplined
     6 Flexible/Determined
    	7 Urgent/Patient
     8 Independent/Protective
     9 Impulsive/Reliable
     T Elusive/Honorable

2	Compassionate	Ruthless
23	Tolerant	Judgmental

     Clubs:
     Courageous
     Resilient
     Persevering
     Determined
     Bold
     Optimistic
     Confident
     Enthusiastic
     Vigilant

     Diamonds:
     Prudent
     Wise
     Curious
     Insightful
     Discerning
     Foresighted
     Knowledgeable
     Clear-minded
     Open-minded
     Resourceful
     Focused

     Hearts:
     Kind
     Empathetic
     Generous
     Charitable
     Forgiving
     Grateful
     Merciful
     Gentle
     Patient
     Selfless

     Spades:
     Just
     Honorable
     Honest
     Fair
     Righteous
     Trustworthy
     Accountable
     Pure
     Altruistic
     Temperate  
     Diligent  
     Disciplined
     Principled")
  (base/rule
   :name "Walk"
   :summary
    "Move up to half of your Starting Speed this Round
     * [Ability] - Walk Abilities keyed to a terrain (eg Walk:Water) allow the user to ignore the movement penalties while walking through the given terrain")
  (base/rule
   :name "Wall"
   :summary
    "A Wall is a type of terrain
     * [Ability] - Wall Abilities keyed to a terrain (eg Wall:Fire) allow the user to place a terrain of the given type (eg Terrain:Fire) of the given type
     * [Area] - The Area can be increased by using Area rules")
  (base/rule
   :name "Weapon:Barehanded"
   :image "images/rule-weapon-barehanded.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Weapon:Improvised"
   :image "images/rule-weapon-improvised.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather"
   :image "images/rule-weather.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Clouds"
   :image "images/rule-weather-clouds.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Downpour")
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Humidity"
   :image "images/rule-weather-humidity.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Hurricane")
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Rain"
   :summary
    "* Dew
     * Dizzle
     * Rain
     * Downpour")
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Snow"
   :summary
    "* Sleet
     * Snowy
     * Snowstorm
     * Blizzard")
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Temperature"
   :image "images/rule-weather-temperature.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Tornado")
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Thunderstorm"
   :image "images/rule-weather-thunderstorm.svg"
   :summary
    "* Conditions: Stormy Humid+ Windy+
     * [Event]: Every 6 hours, [Reveal Fate].
     ** IF a Black Wild THEN a nearby lightning strike
     ** IF a Red Wild THEN a direct lightning strike
     ** Effects - A lightning bolt holds 5 GigaJoules or 5x9 damage for a direct strike, but most lightning strikes go through smaller feelers or are splashes. Even a direct strike is survivable because it usually travels across the surface of the skin instead of through the body.")
  (base/rule
   :name "Weather:Wind"
   :image "images/rule-weather-wind.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
  (base/rule
   :name "Will"
   :image "images/rule-will.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly
   :titles
    "Emotion, Social, Water, Hearts, Cups, Bravery, Chi, Confidence, Courage, Determination, Ego, Faith, Grit, Guts, Heart, Instinct, Ki, Mana, Perseverence, Psychological, Resolve, Spirit, Spiritualism, Willpower"
   :reference
    "* I think, therefore I am. - Descartes, Cogito Ergo Sum
     * The nature of existence is subjective. I have experience and thoughts in this precise moment, beyond that I can prove nothing. Does time actually pass as I understand it? Is anything else but me real? Am I living in a dream/hallucination/simulation? Am I just insane? Our experience is the only thing we can be sure of. Therefore, we may as well choose to live as we see fit. No amount of evidence can definitively prove otherwise.")
  (base/rule
   :name "Withdraw"
   :image "images/rule-withdraw.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly)
))

(func deck-rules : base/deck
 [tactics : base/tactics]
 (let : base/deck
  [cardlist : base/cardlist :=
    (base/cardlist
     (list<-list : base/cardlist
      (base/rulelist<-tactics-keys
       tactics
       "Drawn to Destiny"
       "Disclaimer"
       "How to Play"
       "Description"
       "Features"
       "Golden Rules"
       "Terms"
       "Unit:Sample"
       "Unit:Guide"
       "Item:Sample"
       "Item:Guide"
       "Stat"
       "How to Play"
       "Setup"
       "Setup:Players"
       "Scene"
       "Scene:Map#1"
       "Scene:Map#2"
       "Scene:Minis"
       "Scene:Units"
       "Scene:Events"
       "Round:Start"
       "Move"
       "Movement"
       "Action"
       "Action:Free"
       "Action:Interact"
       "Arc"
       "Range"
       "Line of Sight"
       "Conflict"
       "Conflict:Chart"
       "Conflict:Sample"
       "Hits"
       "Hits:Sample"
       "Crits"
       "Crits:Rating"
       "Crits:Damage"
       "Crits:Types"
       "Crits:Person"
       "Crits:Vehicle"
       "Resolution"
       "Round:End"
       "Conclusion"
       "Advancement"
      )))
   cardmap : base/cardmap :=
    (base/cardmap<-cardlist
     cardlist)]
  (base/deck
   :id "deckrules"
   :name "Rules"
   :image "images/rule-drawntodestiny.svg"
   :layout base/cardlayout-imageonly
   :cardmap cardmap)))

(func tactics-rulemap<-tactics : base/tactics
 [tactics : base/tactics]
 (let : base/tactics
  [rulemap : base/rulemap :=
   (rulemap-tactics tactics)]
  (copy tactics
   :rulemap rulemap))
 :doc "Returns a tactics updated with rulemap")
